WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
A cup of tea sits in a room
at twenty degrees Celsius.

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:07.170
At first, the thermometer
reading drops quickly.

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.260
Later it creeps down
towards room temperature,

4
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.170
and never goes below it.

5
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.810
So what equation says it
cools faster when it's hotter?

6
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.490
The same drop every minute?

7
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.460
Faster as time goes on?

8
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:24.080
In this mission, you'll write how fast
the temperature changes as a derivative,

9
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.880
d T by d t.

10
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.260
You'll turn a sentence about rates
into a differential equation,

11
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.000
which links a function
and its derivatives.

12
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.190
And you'll solve equations like this
when the variables are separable.

13
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.250
Your mission: find the equation for a
drink that cools faster the hotter it is.
